{
  "$comment": "Conformance cases for the `environment.inspect` payload (`GET /api/v1/environment`), added by protocol 1.2 with issues #43 and #44 (the `workspace` path arrived with the workspace it points at). Validated against fenixspoon.core.discovery.EnvironmentInfo by server/tests/test_protocol_fixtures.py. Not read by the JS SDK's conformance suite: discovery serves local callers \u2014 scripts, a CLI, an agent over JSON-RPC \u2014 and the browser SDK does not implement it, so there are no two sides here to drift apart. The moment the SDK grows a typed `inspectEnvironment`, it reads this file and the drift guard applies as it does for the other corpora.",
